A free particle, one that experiences no forces, moves with constant velocity in an inertial frame:
$
  bold(dot(v)) = bold(dot.double(x)) = bold(0).
$

The law of inertia is an improved version of Newton's 1st law. Rather than singling out a natural state of rest that forces maintain or disturb, it asserts uniform motion of free particles in every inertial frame; being at rest is itself just constant velocity in a suitable frame.
